<title>INDIA: India to launch new satellite on June 4.</title>
<headline>India to launch new satellite on June 4.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's newest satellite, INSAT-2D, will be launched on June 4, a government statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The launch will be aboard the Ariane rocket, at 0430 hrs (Indian Standard Time), the statement added.</p>
<p>The satellite has been built by the Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) and will be launched from Kourou in French Guyana.</p>
<p>The multi-purpose geostationary satellite can be used for meterology and communication.</p>
<p>- New Delhi Newsroom +91 11 301 2024</p>
